{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373896032,"sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"skill","callID":"call_8bbb42a70550486ebff3a555","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"name":"pyasc-cannbench-kernel"},"output":"<skill_content name=\"pyasc-cannbench-kernel\">\n# Skill: pyasc-cannbench-kernel\n\n# pyasc v2 CANNBench kernel workflow\n\nUse this skill only for the vendored benchmark under\n`integrations/cannbench/`. Its compact module contract overrides the generic\nstandalone-kernel workflow.\n\n## Non-negotiable contract\n\n- Treat `tasks/<op>/proto.yaml`, `golden.py`, and all 20 entries in\n  `cases.yaml` as one indivisible specification.\n- Produce one `candidate.py` with the exact top-level callable and defaults.\n- Use `torch` only for allocation, metadata views, and launches. Numerical work\n  belongs in one or more `@asc2.jit` kernels.\n- Import and call `ensure_npu_platform` from `._pyasc_runtime`.\n- Target `Ascend950PR_9599`, at most 72 vector cores, and UB capacity 253952 B.\n- For the pinned runtime use `asc2.global_tensor`, `asc2.copy_in`, and\n  `asc2.copy_out`; use `real_shape` for tails. Do not substitute the older\n  `tensor/load/store` spelling.\n- Treat padded lanes as executed lanes: choose an explicit, operation-neutral\n  `pad_value` for `real_shape` loads (especially `1` for divisors) so tail\n  arithmetic does not create avoidable Inf/NaN exceptions.\n- A production candidate normally uses bare `@asc2.jit` or an evidenced\n  allocation option. `always_compile=True` is a development aid, not a\n  submission requirement.\n\n## Required workflow\n\n1. Read the three task files and summarize every dtype, rank, attribute, list\n   arity, special value, and boundary shape. Do not optimize for one example.\n   An upstream target test is a useful implementation reference, not evidence\n   that its narrower dtype/shape/attribute domain implements this contract.\n2. Read [operator patterns](references/operator-patterns.md), selecting only\n   the target operator section.\n3. Design host dispatch, kernel specializations, tails, dtype conversions, UB\n   budget, and numerical behavior before writing code.\n4. Implement the exact callable. Run `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and\n   the worker static contract check.\n5. Run the exact-v2 local compile gate for that operator as described in\n   [local validation](references/local-validation.md). A compile failure is\n   measured feedback; repair it and re-run all 20 cases.\n6. For numerically sensitive formulas, run the adversarial camodel smoke when\n   the native runtime is available. It must exercise both ordinary and\n   special-value routes using the task's dtype-specific tolerances. Treat a\n   small all-finite smoke as insufficient for promotion.\n7. Have a different available model review the task, design, candidate, and\n   local report. Record both model IDs, OpenCode session IDs, loaded skill\n   source hashes, prompt/design/candidate hashes, and gate results.\n\nNever claim numerical correctness or performance from the local compile gate.\nOnly camodel execution can provide local numerical evidence; only CANNBench on\nthe real NPU is the acceptance/performance oracle.\n\n## Evidence labels\n\nUse exactly one label for every conclusion:\n\n- `verified-local-compile`: all task routes lower through pinned pyasc v2.\n- `verified-camodel-smoke`: the stated representative routes executed and\n  matched their golden; scope must list omitted dtypes/shapes/cases.\n- `verified-camodel`: outputs were executed and compared to the task golden.\n- `verified-cannbench`: official hardware result and case count are recorded.\n- `suspected`: evidence is incomplete or the root cause is inferred.\n\nDo not promote a locally qualified candidate into the canonical submission\npackage without numerical evidence. When a CANNBench run reports case-level\nfailures, feed those exact case IDs and failure classes into repair; a clean\ncompile matrix must never override measured numerical failures. Do not spend a\nsubmission credit unless the user explicitly enables remote evaluation.\n\n## Known limitations\n\nBefore using a workaround, consult\n[pyasc v2 blockers](references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md). Preserve full case\ncoverage when a case exposes a compiler limit; never remove or shrink the case\nto make a gate pass.\n\nBase directory for this skill: /home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel\nRelative paths in this skill (e.g., scripts/, reference/) are relative to this base directory.\nNote: file list is sampled.\n\n<skill_files>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/local-validation.md</file>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/pyasc-v2-blockers.md</file>\n<file>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel/references/operator-patterns.md</file>\n</skill_files>\n</skill_content>","metadata":{"name":"pyasc-cannbench-kernel","dir":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/skills/pyasc-cannbench-kernel","truncated":false},"title":"Loaded skill: pyasc-cannbench-kernel","time":{"start":1788373896023,"end":1788373896031}},"id":"prt_063640ac90014b6i1pmOzuZR27","sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","messageID":"msg_06363ffc1001ZI2x0511MYWsN1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373896626,"sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_bf05e3d0fda74574921d0a50","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n2: \n3: Repair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\n4: must remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n5: `gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n6: \n7: The candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n8: `job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n9: \n10: - case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n11: - case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n12: - case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n13: - case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n14: \n15: BF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n16: `1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n17: `pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\n18: copy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\n19: all dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\n20: only `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n21: \n\n(End of file - total 21 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","text":"# Repair task: CANNBench GELU after real 950PR feedback\n\nRepair `candidate.py` for the vendored CANNBench GELU contract. Numerical work\nmust remain in pyasc v2 `@asc2.jit` kernels and the public signature remains\n`gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor`.\n\nThe candidate already passes the exact-v2 compile matrix, but private 950PR job\n`job_ae3bfdefd087` passed only 16/20. All failures are FP32 precision failures:\n\n- case 5, tanh, range [-100, 100]: MERE 9.008301e-4;\n- case 8, tanh, range [-5, 10]: MERE 0.003110;\n- case 11, exact, range [-88, 88]: MERE 0.002386;\n- case 20, exact, range [-20, 40]: MERE 0.006894.\n\nBF16 Inf/NaN case 12 passes in this seed and must remain passing. The direct\n`1 + erf/tanh` forms cancel in negative tails. Apply the updated\n`pyasc-cannbench-kernel` skill's 950PR-verified stable GELU formulations. Do not\ncopy or inspect the repository's canonical submission implementation. Preserve\nall dtypes, tails, attributes and special-value semantics. After editing, run\nonly `python3 -m py_compile candidate.py` and end with `REPAIR_DONE`.\n","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":21,"totalLines":21,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/task.md","time":{"start":1788373896612,"end":1788373896622}},"id":"prt_063640bea001oxFU1NZBRu3xd7","sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","messageID":"msg_06363ffc1001ZI2x0511MYWsN1"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788373897181,"sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_2a5293fb915342b1937ee775","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py"},"output":"<path>/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: \"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n2: \n3: Kernel design (grid-stride variant):\n4:   - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n5:   - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n6:   - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n7:     spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n8:     store.\n9:   - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n10:     param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n11:       * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n12:             y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n13:       * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n14:             y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n15:   - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n16:     on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n17:   - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n18:     1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n19:   - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n20:     values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n21:     identical-form evaluation.\n22: \"\"\"\n23: \n24: import math\n25: \n26: import torch\n27: \n28: import asc\n29: import asc2\n30: \n31: from ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n32: \n33: _C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n34: _C0_TANH = math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n35: _K_TANH = 0.044715\n36: \n37: _ERF_TILE = 2048\n38: _NARROW_TILE = 1024\n39: _TANH_TILE = 1024\n40: _MAX_CORES = 72\n41: _ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n42: \n43: \n44: @asc2.jit\n45: def _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n46:                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n47:                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n48:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n49:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n50:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n51:                         unroll_factor=2):\n52:         off = t * tile_size\n53:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n54:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n55:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n56:         s = xf * _C1_ERF\n57:         e = asc2.erf(s)\n58:         one = e + 1.0\n59:         hx = xf * 0.5\n60:         yf = hx * one\n61:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n62: \n63: \n64: @asc2.jit\n65: def _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n66:                       size: int, num_tiles: int,\n67:                       tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n68:     x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n69:     out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n70:     for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n71:                         unroll_factor=2):\n72:         off = t * tile_size\n73:         n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n74:         x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n75:         xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n76:         x2 = xf * xf\n77:         x3 = x2 * xf\n78:         a = x3 * _K_TANH\n79:         b = xf + a\n80:         c = b * _C0_TANH\n81:         th = asc2.tanh(c)\n82:         one = th + 1.0\n83:         hx = xf * 0.5\n84:         yf = hx * one\n85:         asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n86: \n87: \n88: def gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n89:     \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n90:     ensure_npu_platform()\n91:     assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n92:         f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n93:     if not x.is_contiguous():\n94:         x = x.contiguous()\n95:     out = torch.empty_like(x)\n96:     size = x.numel()\n97:     if size == 0:\n98:         return out\n99:     if approximate == \"none\":\n100:         if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n101:             tile = _ERF_TILE\n102:         else:\n103:             tile = _NARROW_TILE\n104:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n105:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n106:         _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n107:     else:\n108:         tile = _TANH_TILE\n109:         num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n110:         cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n111:         _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n112:     return out\n\n(End of file - total 112 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/home/aloschilov/workspace/pyasc-skill-stack/integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","text":"\"\"\"CANN Bench Gelu interface implemented as a pyasc asc2 kernel.\n\nKernel design (grid-stride variant):\n  - 1-D flatten; each block strides over tiles so any element count / rank works.\n  - Tail tiles handled with ``real_shape`` loads/stores (no host padding).\n  - f16/bf16 inputs are promoted to f32 inside the kernel for precision (the\n    spec's precision standard expects f32 internal compute), then cast back on\n    store.\n  - Host dispatches on the ``approximate`` string (unsupported as a kernel\n    param) to one of two specialized ``@asc2.jit`` kernels:\n      * erf mode  (approximate == \"none\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (erf(x / sqrt(2)) + 1.0)\n      * tanh mode (approximate == \"tanh\"):\n            y = (x * 0.5) * (tanh(sqrt(2/pi) * (x + 0.044715 * x^3)) + 1.0)\n  - All constants are module-level floats (no math.* inside jit); scalars stay\n    on the RIGHT of tile arithmetic (Tile has no __rmul__).\n  - Tiles: erf chain (V~6) uses 2048 wide / 1024 narrow; tanh chain (V~10) uses\n    1024 (UB-budget safe under 253952 B with unroll_factor=2).\n  - erf/tanh are bounded ops, so no overflow guard is needed; IEEE special\n    values (Inf/NaN) propagate through the vector ops and match the golden's\n    identical-form evaluation.\n\"\"\"\n\nimport math\n\nimport torch\n\nimport asc\nimport asc2\n\nfrom ._pyasc_runtime import ensure_npu_platform\n\n_C1_ERF = 1.0 / math.sqrt(2.0)\n_C0_TANH = math.sqrt(2.0 / math.pi)\n_K_TANH = 0.044715\n\n_ERF_TILE = 2048\n_NARROW_TILE = 1024\n_TANH_TILE = 1024\n_MAX_CORES = 72\n_ERF_THRESHOLD = _MAX_CORES * _ERF_TILE\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_erf_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                     size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                     tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        s = xf * _C1_ERF\n        e = asc2.erf(s)\n        one = e + 1.0\n        hx = xf * 0.5\n        yf = hx * one\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\n@asc2.jit\ndef _gelu_tanh_kernel(x_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress, out_ptr: asc.GlobalAddress,\n                      size: int, num_tiles: int,\n                      tile_size: asc.ConstExpr[int]):\n    x_gm = asc2.global_tensor(x_ptr, [size])\n    out_gm = asc2.global_tensor(out_ptr, [size])\n    for t in asc2.range(asc2.block_idx(), num_tiles, asc2.block_num(),\n                        unroll_factor=2):\n        off = t * tile_size\n        n = tile_size if off + tile_size <= size else size - off\n        x = asc2.copy_in(x_gm, [off], [tile_size], real_shape=[n])\n        xf = x.to(asc.float32)\n        x2 = xf * xf\n        x3 = x2 * xf\n        a = x3 * _K_TANH\n        b = xf + a\n        c = b * _C0_TANH\n        th = asc2.tanh(c)\n        one = th + 1.0\n        hx = xf * 0.5\n        yf = hx * one\n        asc2.copy_out(yf.to(x.dtype), out_gm, [off], real_shape=[n])\n\n\ndef gelu(x: torch.Tensor, approximate: str = \"none\") -> torch.Tensor:\n    \"\"\"Element-wise GELU of an NPU tensor via a pyasc asc2 kernel.\"\"\"\n    ensure_npu_platform()\n    assert approximate in (\"none\", \"tanh\"), (\n        f\"approximate must be 'none' or 'tanh', got {approximate!r}\")\n    if not x.is_contiguous():\n        x = x.contiguous()\n    out = torch.empty_like(x)\n    size = x.numel()\n    if size == 0:\n        return out\n    if approximate == \"none\":\n        if size >= _ERF_THRESHOLD:\n            tile = _ERF_TILE\n        else:\n            tile = _NARROW_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_erf_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    else:\n        tile = _TANH_TILE\n        num_tiles = asc.ceildiv(size, tile)\n        cores = min(_MAX_CORES, num_tiles)\n        _gelu_tanh_kernel[cores](x, out, size, num_tiles, tile)\n    return out","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":112,"totalLines":112,"truncated":false}},"title":"integrations/cannbench/comparisons/target-intersection-20260902/correction/with_skills/work/candidate.py","time":{"start":1788373897165,"end":1788373897177}},"id":"prt_063640dfb001aRl9yEOL5aoLjj","sessionID":"ses_f9c9c0115ffeqVStPv7eXLORPJ","messageID":"msg_06363ffc1001ZI2x0511MYWsN1"}}
